<%# locals: goal %>
<% return unless goal.life_stage_pregnancy? %>
<section class="card day-card mb-3 border-info border-opacity-25">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h2 class="h5 mb-1">Pregnancy movement</h2>
    <p class="small text-muted mb-2">
      Based on <%= GestationalWeightGuidance::EXERCISE_SOURCE_LABEL %>.
      Not medical advice — follow your clinician.
    </p>
    <% unless goal.exercise_cleared_by_clinician? %>
      <div class="alert alert-warning small mb-2 py-2">
        Mark “cleared for exercise” in <%= link_to "Goals", edit_goal_path %> after your clinician confirms.
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <ul class="small mb-2">
      <li>Aim for ~<strong>150 minutes/week</strong> of moderate-intensity aerobic activity when cleared.</li>
      <li>Strength training is generally OK with modifications; avoid breath-holding / Valsalva strain.</li>
      <li>After the first trimester, avoid prolonged <strong>supine</strong> (flat on your back) exercise.</li>
      <li>Stop and seek care for: vaginal bleeding, regular painful contractions, amniotic fluid leakage,
        dizziness, chest pain, calf pain/swelling, headache, muscle weakness affecting balance, or decreased fetal movement.</li>
      <li>Don’t invent “safe 1RM %” from this app — reduce load when form or symptoms change, and ask your OB/physio for personal limits.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Keep logging runs, walks, and lifts as usual — the history helps postpartum recovery.</p>
  </div>
</section>
